tesseract.js 7.0.0 in Orisod: notice for its engine, the code it bundles and its language data

This file was written by Orisod. Every other file in this folder is an
unmodified copy of its upstream source (see assets/vendor/manifest.json).

Orisod's OCR PDF tool (/ocr-pdf/ and /es/ocr-pdf/) loads these files from this
folder instead of from cdnjs and jsDelivr. The page passes Tesseract the full
addresses of the worker (workerPath), of the core folder (corePath) and of the
lang folder (langPath), so nothing is downloaded from another server.

1. tesseract.js 7.0.0, Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE)
   tesseract.min.js and worker.min.js, identical to dist/ in the npm package
   tesseract.js@7.0.0 (tesseract.min.js is also the file on cdnjs).
   Source code: https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js/tree/v7.0.0
   worker.min.js bundles buffer (MIT), ieee754 (BSD-3-Clause), regenerator-runtime
   (MIT) and zlib.js (MIT); their notices are in worker.min.js.LICENSE.txt, as
   published next to it. tesseract.min.js.LICENSE.txt is the one published next
   to tesseract.min.js.

2. tesseract.js-core 7.0.0, Apache License 2.0 (core/LICENSE)
   The OCR engine, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Each .wasm.js file
   holds its WebAssembly inside it, so it fetches no other file. tesseract.js
   7.0.0 runs the LSTM-only engine by default, and its worker picks one of these
   three builds by what the browser supports:
     core/tesseract-core-relaxedsimd-lstm.wasm.js  (relaxed SIMD)
     core/tesseract-core-simd-lstm.wasm.js         (SIMD)
     core/tesseract-core-lstm.wasm.js              (neither)
   The package's other builds (with the legacy engine, or as separate .wasm
   files) are never loaded by the OCR PDF tool and aren't included.
   Source code: https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js-core/tree/v7.0.0
