3. Language data: lang/eng.traineddata.gz (English page) and
   lang/spa.traineddata.gz (Spanish page)
   These are the 4.0.0_best_int files of the npm packages
   @tesseract.js-data/eng@1.0.0 and @tesseract.js-data/spa@1.0.0, the same files
   tesseract.js 7.0.0 downloads by default from
   https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tesseract.js-data/<lang>/4.0.0_best_int/
   They come from the project https://github.com/naptha/tessdata, which takes
   the models of Tesseract's tessdata_best (https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best),
   turns them into LSTM-only integer models with Tesseract's combine_tessdata
   tool and compresses them with gzip (its gzip-integerize-traineddata.sh).
   - tessdata_best is licensed under the Apache License 2.0:
     lang/LICENSE-tessdata_best is its LICENSE at commit
     e12c65a915945e4c28e237a9b52bc4a8f39a0cec.
   - naptha/tessdata is licensed under the Apache License 2.0:
     lang/LICENSE-naptha-tessdata is its LICENSE at commit
     806cd9adc8c6e8abc11c782db1818c990576bebc.
   - The npm packages @tesseract.js-data/eng and @tesseract.js-data/spa declare
     the MIT license in their package.json ("license": "MIT", author Balearica)
     but contain no license text. lang/package-eng.json and lang/package-spa.json
     are those package.json files, unmodified, as the record of that
     declaration.
   tesseract.js decompresses the .gz file itself (it checks for the gzip
   header), and caches the result in the browser's IndexedDB under the same
   name as before ("./eng.traineddata" or "./spa.traineddata").
